WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.190
SAVANNAH MAZIYA: I think the
smartest people in the world

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:12.180
are people who are going to be
looking to invest in Africa.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:18.788
Africa as a whole is really very well
known as a resource-rich environment.

00:00:18.788 --> 00:00:21.330
ROBERT BROZIN: We knew nothing
about the restaurant business.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:26.790
And my original intention was really
to do it as part of a pure investment.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.540
JAMES MWANGI: We're
able to digitize that.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.110
We're be able to create
algorithms because we

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.630
have data spanning thirty years.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:39.170
There has been a lot of
movement or transformation.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.820
Very micro businesses becomes more--

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.120
more businesses become medium.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.520
Medium become large enterprises.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.530
And large enterprises are corporatizing.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.530
SAVANNAH MAZIYA: You can't
keep pointing fingers

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.660
and say someone's going
to come and save the day.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.820
You have to, in your own
way, figure out a way

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.467
to lead and let others
join you or assist you.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:00:59.675
But be part of that solution.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.489
JAMES MWANGI: They are
in the driver's seat.

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:09.320
We're just empowering them
to change their lives.

